===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|St. Vincent and the Grenadines|St Vincent and the Grenadines|St. Vincent & the Grenadines|St Vincent & the Grenadines}}

===Etymology===
After Saint Vincent (sighted by [[Columbus]] on St Vincent's Day, 22 January 1498) and the city of [[Granada]] in Spain.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/seɪnt ˈvɪnt.sənt ən ðə ˈɡɹɛn.əˌdiːnz/|/- ˌɡɹɛn.əˈdiːnz/||a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Saint Vincent and the Grenadines.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[Saint Vincent]] [[and]] [[the]] [[Grenadines]]}}

# {{senseid|en|Q757}}{{place|en|archipelago/and/country|r/Caribbean}}, comprising the islands of [[Saint Vincent]] and the island chain of the [[Grenadines]].

